<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chandragupta I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 320 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chandragupta I was the ruler who established the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gupta-empire">Gupta Empire</a> as a major power in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> around 320 CE. He took the title of maharajadhiraja and strengthened his position through marriage to a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/licchavi">Licchavi</a> princess. His reign began the expansion continued by his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samudragupta">Samudragupta</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chandragupta-i.jpg" alt="Chandragupta I" width="320" height="327" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Uploadalt · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Queen_Kumaradevi_and_King_Chandragupta_I_on_a_coin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
